# Handbook — update with the code

Committed `docs/` is how this project is explained. Gitignored `docs/secrets-and-access.md` and `MAINTAINER.local.md` hold passwords and live stamps.

## After every product change (same turn)

1. Identify which handbook files the change touches (table below).
2. Edit those files so they match **source**, not memory. Cite real action names, setting keys, tables, routes.
3. If a password, token, Worker version, or D1 stamp changed: `docs/secrets-and-access.md` and/or `MAINTAINER.local.md`.
4. Do **not** `git add docs/secrets-and-access.md` or `MAINTAINER.local.md`.
5. If those secrets files are missing on this machine, say so. Do not invent live IDs.

For any page or RBAC change, keep the complete view/action matrix synchronized in `docs/pages-and-ui.md` and `docs/auth-rbac.md`. A page-level `canView*` key is only an entry gate; document and test create, edit, delete, payment, workflow, and destructive action permissions separately.

Before committing, inspect staged and unstaged diffs. Product behavior changes must include their matching documentation and focused tests in the same commit; never commit source-only RBAC/API/page changes. Run `git diff --cached --check` and the applicable validation commands before pushing.

Skip only for pure comment/format/typo-in-code with zero behavior change.

## Which file

| You changed | Update |
|-------------|--------|
| `schema.ts` / `migrations/` | `docs/data-model.md`, `docs/schema-columns.md`, `docs/relationships.md` |
| `api/**/route.ts` or `action` strings | `docs/api-map.md`; RBAC maps → `docs/auth-rbac.md` |
| Check-in / Vision / Drive | `docs/flows-guest-checkin.md`, `docs/interactions.md` |
| Food / kitchen / stock | `docs/flows-food-kitchen.md` |
| Beds / bookings / inventory / Aiosell | `docs/flows-pms.md`, `docs/llm-onboarding.md` if a landmine |
| Expenses / ledger / salary | `docs/flows-accounts.md` |
| Staff/volunteer splits | `docs/flows-splits.md` |
| Website CMS / R2 | `docs/flows-cms.md` |
| Sync / Pi | `docs/flows-sync.md` |
| Reviews / Form C | `docs/flows-reviews-formc.md` |
| Auth / permissions | `docs/auth-rbac.md` |
| Env secrets / logins | `docs/secrets-and-access.md` (gitignored) |
| Env **names** | `docs/env-vars.md` |
| Deploy / D1 applied list | `MAINTAINER.local.md` |
| New top-level concept | `docs/overview.md` / `docs/architecture.md` / `docs/decisions.md` / `docs/developing.md` |
| Folder layout / lib / admin UI | `docs/directory.md`, `docs/pages-and-ui.md` |
| Tests / CI | `docs/testing-and-ci.md` |

Index: `docs/README.md`. New agent: `docs/llm-onboarding.md` + `docs/developing.md`. Dedicated pass: skill `goko-local-docs`. Project-wide agent instructions also live in the repository root `AGENTS.md` and apply to every chat/agent working in GokoWeb.

If you change a landmine (array wire format, permission mismatch, occupancy split, `useAdminApi` target), update `docs/llm-onboarding.md`.
